                      },
                      "group": "",
                      "groupIndex": 0,
                      "text": "Dew point indicates moisture comfort better than relative humidity. Based on NOAA comfort scale. It shows how muggy or dry the air feels. Low dew point means dry air causing skin and respiratory irritation. High dew point feels sticky and oppressive, making it hard to cool down through sweating. Ideal range provides comfortable breathing and natural cooling.",
                      "textType": "literal",
                      "longMode": "WRAP",
                      "recolor": false
                    },
                    {
                      "objID": "59f07008-b6ce-4078-9502-6ea6317d4bbc",
