                              }
                            }
                          },
                          "group": "",
                          "groupIndex": 0,
                          "text": "PM1 are ultrafine particles smaller than 1 micron that penetrate deepest into lungs and enter bloodstream directly. Sources: combustion, vehicle exhaust, tobacco smoke, cooking fumes. Most dangerous particle size due to deep tissue penetration. No official EPA thresholds exist, values derived from PM2.5 guidelines with stricter limits due to increased health impact.",
                          "textType": "literal",
                          "longMode": "WRAP",
                          "recolor": false
                        },
                        {
                          "objID": "1463bcf3-7e00-4143-f454-bd8b3eb46c14",
