                            }
                          },
                          "group": "",
                          "groupIndex": 0,
                          "text": "PM10 are coarse particles including dust, pollen, and mold spores. Thresholds based on US EPA Air Quality Index (AQI). Can irritate eyes, nose, and throat. Less harmful than PM2.5 but still affects respiratory health. Sources: dust, construction, pollen, road particles. Reduce through regular cleaning, air filtration, and keeping windows closed.",
                          "textType": "literal",
                          "longMode": "WRAP",
                          "recolor": false
                        },
