                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "group": "",
                  "groupIndex": 0,
                  "text": "Carbon monoxide is an odorless, colorless toxic gas from incomplete combustion. Sources: gas stoves, heaters, fireplaces, vehicle exhaust, tobacco smoke. CO blocks oxygen delivery in blood, causing headaches, dizziness, and death at high levels. Thresholds based on WHO and EPA guidelines. Ensure proper ventilation when using combustion appliances. Install CO detector for safety.",
                  "textType": "literal",
                  "longMode": "WRAP",
                  "recolor": false
                },
